BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (commercial invoice, packing slip and 7501. The export side needs the invoice, packing slip and proof of export: a bill) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (of lading, B3/CAD, pedimento, airway bill or seaway bill. Inventory receipt and withdrawal dates complete the packet,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (and a manufacturing application adds production in/out dates and the bill of materials [SO9sA-x5K0k @ 00:29:46].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (CEDA accepts paper records and has flown staff to clients to collect them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Refund size is engineered through accounting method and matching logic, not just paperwork. Monica Pascarella walks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (through six accounting methods: FIFO, LIFO, low-to-high, low-to-high average inventory turnover, low-to-high) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (blanket and average. Low-to-high blanket is the most common, but 'not always' the highest recovery [1_L7fnmAAU0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (@ 00:11:41]. The Flexport team adds two levers. Grouping entry lines lowers per-unit duty, and importers who moved) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (sourcing out of China should switch from low-to-high to FIFO [1_L7fnmAAU0 @ 00:32:02]. On substitution, J2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (matching runs HTS-to-HTS off ACE data, claiming the highest duty first. Alex Neutloff shows why the matching) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (engine matters. A greedy algorithm yields 11 where the optimal match yields 70. A 10-by-10 matching problem carries) Tj ET
