BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 557.77 Tm (The most expensive failures are clock failures. Jill La Madeleine at International Tariff Management describes a wine) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 542.55 Tm (company that held an approved privilege, went beyond the five years, and 'lost $1,000,000' in recovery [gf35xQR8Lz0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 527.32 Tm (@ 00:08:37]. Scarbrough Global's Pat Caulfield and Adam name the single biggest pitfall: missing CBP information) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 512.10 Tm (requests inside the 5-year window, which sinks claims that were otherwise filed on time [wEYqdvTPaqM @ 00:30:38].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 496.87 Tm (The same Scarbrough team warns that the one-time retroactive waiver forces a decision. You have to 'pick a day' for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 481.65 Tm (the Notice of Intent before anything else, or bleed 3 to 6 months of eligible imports off the back end of the look-back) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 466.42 Tm ([wEYqdvTPaqM @ 00:32:45]. CEDA's countermeasure, presented at World Trade Center Denver, is to file claims the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 451.20 Tm (same day the privilege application is submitted. That locks the 5-year window counted from each import date. CEDA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 435.97 Tm (targets 90 days from contract signing to first claim, then 3 to 18 months for CBP approval and about 45 days per claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 420.75 Tm (to payment afterward [SO9sA-x5K0k @ 00:33:40]. CEDA also reports that CBP kept working during the government) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 405.52 Tm (shutdown but Treasury refund payments paused, so a perfectly timed claim can still sit unpaid.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 390.30 Tm (Data mismatches are the second failure cluster, and they surface at filing rather than at audit. Allison Shower at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.07 Tm (Scarbrough Global reports that claim data must match ACE exactly, down to unit of measure. Shower recounts a claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 359.85 Tm (rejected over a post-summary correction nobody on the drawback side had seen [6Ogi9iKVSTE @ 00:21:06]. Shower's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 344.62 Tm (rule is to resolve PSCs and protests, and let Reconciliation run its 21 months, before filing. Shower also warns that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 329.40 Tm ('almost every time you file your first claim you are going to get hit with a full desk review.' Joe Harper at Star USA,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.17 Tm (Inc. adds the mechanical checks: use the 10-digit HTS with matching units of measure, and upload supporting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 298.95 Tm (documents within 24 hours [NK99CBNOeJA @ 00:30:49]. Classification is the deeper trap. Scarbrough Global warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 283.72 Tm (that 'other/other/other' lines are a 'big swath of lots of potential issues' and exactly where importers 'get in trouble,' even) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 268.50 Tm (when the duty-free result 'looks great' [fI28fmPlbPA @ 00:04:40]. Scarbrough's Caulfield and Adam tie audit risk to) Tj ET
