BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.77 Tm (Flexport's Tom Gould names flash title as the fastest way to lose a first sale claim: when both sales are set up FOB) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.55 Tm (Hong Kong and title moves on both at the same instant, customs has often ruled the middleman never truly owned the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.32 Tm (goods, so working programs build in a separate title transfer to the middleman, even one lasting less than a day, before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 352.10 Tm (the second transfer to the importer [yR_RXKhapxo @ 00:15:27]. Diversion is the second killer. A purchase order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.87 Tm (splitting 100,000 units between Canada and the US fails, and multilingual labels or certifications for several destination) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.65 Tm (countries can let customs invalidate the claim outright [yR_RXKhapxo @ 00:18:24]. Ask The Customs Manager) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.42 Tm (supplies the inverse proof: factory-printed country-specific safety labels, language tags or your corporate logo show the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 291.20 Tm (goods were destined for you at the moment of sale, and you cannot guess the factory price because customs heavily) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.97 Tm (audits the strategy [5fk-EKpR8Zw @ 00:01:26]. Anna Zjack of Flexport flags a quieter trap: distributor agreements) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.75 Tm (carrying consigned inventory or post-delivery conditions can undercut a bona fide sale even when the invoice incoterm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.52 Tm (looks clean, because incoterms do not settle ownership and title often transfers only after the boat is on the water) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.30 Tm ([yR_RXKhapxo @ 00:44:21].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.07 Tm (The money leaks Tom Gould has watched companies walk into come from additions. When an importer declares the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.85 Tm (first sale, it must add assists, royalties and proceeds of subsequent sale tied to that first sale even when the middleman) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.62 Tm (paid them, such as fabric the middleman hands the factory free, and Gould says this is exactly where companies get in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.40 Tm (trouble when no process feeds those numbers to the broker; a ruling on a representative transaction is no blanket shield) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.17 Tm (either, because customs compares every later entry against it for differences [yR_RXKhapxo @ 00:34:06]. Steve Cork) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.95 Tm (lists the hidden dutiable items importers miss: pre-shipment testing fees are dutiable whether the buyer or the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.72 Tm (manufacturer pays them, and free samples not written into the sales contract get valued as identical goods) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 108.50 Tm ([mimI2zifsUA @ 00:41:48]. Tooling supplied to a factory must be apportioned over its production life, dividing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 93.27 Tm (cost by five million phones if you expect a million a year for five years [mimI2zifsUA @ 00:57:03]. Customs Directory) Tj ET
